# UI reference captures from live Coretax.
#
# Screenshots carry real taxpayer data (the owner's own identity fields, and
# dependants' names/NIKs/DOBs in L-1 Section C), so images stay local until
# they have been reviewed and redacted.
#
# The written notes are PII-free and are tracked: they are the actual value of
# the capture work, and having them in git history is what makes stale claims
# visible as diffs instead of something to rediscover.
/docs/**/*.jpg
/docs/**/*.jpeg
/docs/**/*.png
/docs/**/*.gif
/docs/**/*.webp
/docs/**/*.pdf

# Raw accessibility-tree dumps stay local: they are verbatim DOM captures and
# contain dependants' names and NIKs (L-1 Section C). The owner's decision to
# leave dependant PII unredacted was conditional on docs/ not being tracked.
# Regenerate from the live form if one is needed; do not commit one.
/docs/**/a11y-*.txt
